Defines the complete setup and business rules for a Point of Sale (POS) session — one record = one POS terminal / store configuration.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Configure POS interface (receipts, payments, discounts, taxes)
Define available payment methods (cash, card, bank transfer, etc.)
Set up hardware (printers, cash drawers, barcode scanners, customer displays)
Control product categories, pricelists, and order management
Enable multi-session, multi-company, and multi-shop operations
Manage loyalty programs, invoicing, and refunds at POS
Restaurant mode (floors, tables, orders)

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), company_id
iface_cashdrawer, iface_printer, iface_electronic_scale, iface_customer_facing_display
payment_method_ids → Many2many to pos.payment.method
journal_id (default sales journal), invoice_journal_id
pricelist_id, available_pricelist_ids
receipt_header, receipt_footer
module_pos_restaurant, module_pos_discount, module_pos_loyalty, etc.
session_ids → One2many to pos.session

Critical Hooks: open_ui, _get_available_payment_methods, onchange_company_id
Security: point_of_sale.group_pos_manager + company rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
POS config, point of sale configuration, pos configuration, pos setup, pos terminal settings, point of sale profile, cash register config, pos payment methods, pos receipt, pos hardware, restaurant pos, pos session config
Related Models (most joined):

pos.session (live sessions)
pos.payment.method
pos.order (via session)
account.journal
product.pricelist
pos.category
res.company

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
pos.config is the main Odoo Point of Sale configuration model that defines terminal settings including payment methods, hardware interfaces (printer, scale, cash drawer), pricelists, journals, receipt templates, and enabled modules (restaurant, loyalty, discount). It controls the entire POS behavior and is the parent of pos.session and pos.order, serving as the central setup for retail, restaurant, and shop operations.